.\n\n\nThe phrase \"kẻ xanh với đường gantt nối xuống\" refers to the blue progress bar and the connecting Gantt line visualized in Image 2. Task addition involves generating this bar and either linking it to the predecessor task or the next task, depending on dependencies. The primary goal is to ensure full 2-way synchronization of data across different views: TasksPage, GanttPage, and HRPage. Analysis suggests that tasks and ganttItems require unification and synchronization from the database model in `db.json`.\n\n\nA new task in `TasksPage` triggers creation in `db.tasks`, finding the employee ID by assignee name, and populates task details including `title`, `phase`, dates, and estimated time. The corresponding entry will be created in `db.ganttItems`, determining the appropriate WBS code and setting unit and color based on the task phase. The new Gantt item's dependencies are automatically linked to the previous task in that phase.\n\n\nExamining the code, the `HEADER_HEIGHT` is applied to the header. The height of the rows and header of the left table and right table needs to match exactly, but there is no specific height defined for the right table header. Inconsistency in header heights leads to misaligned rows, causing offset between chart elements and row labels, impacting visual accuracy.\n\n\nThe left header's height increase stems from text wrapping in its flex container, overriding the initially set `HEADER_HEIGHT`. Flexbox's default `min-height: auto` causes the container to expand to accommodate multi-line content, leading to height differences with the right header. This height discrepancy causes the Gantt chart elements to misalign with the row labels, as the SVG's rendering origin is fixed at the original `HEADER_HEIGHT`.\n\n\nEnsuring consistent header and row heights is crucial to address the observed misalignment. Fixing the header height requires setting a fixed height and preventing text wrapping in the left header. Setting `HEADER_HEIGHT` to 52px and applying fixed heights with `box-border` to all headers aligns the tables.\n\n\nConsistent row heights and the use of `box-border` are essential for precise SVG element alignment.  Calculations for row and gridline coordinates will be based on `ROW_HEIGHT` and `HEADER_HEIGHT`.  Dependencies are automatically linked to the immediately preceding task in the same phase if none are explicitly selected. This is the desired behavior for automatically creating dependencies and displaying the message.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\GiaWyy\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\aps-project-manager\\backend\\data\\db.json","EndLine":60,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"Viewing db.json structure","toolSummary":"View db.json"}}]}
